# Rust build artifacts
/target/
ext/amoskeag/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Keep the workspace Cargo.lock committed for reproducible cross-builds. It
# lives at the root because ext/amoskeag is a workspace *member*: Cargo resolves
# the whole workspace against the root lockfile and never reads a member-level
# one. A stray ext/amoskeag/Cargo.lock is dead weight that silently pins stale
# revisions, so it is ignored rather than committed.
ext/amoskeag/Cargo.lock

